OL,3,GNEWSAWoman jailed for 10 years for     
OL,4,Aexplosives offences                    
OL,6,FIn July she was found guilty of five   
OL,7,Fcounts of causing criminal damage and  
OL,8,Ftwo counts of making an explosive      
OL,9,Fsubstance, but not guilty of attempting
OL,10,Fto cause explosions and of all charges 
OL,11,Frelating to an attack on a transmitting
OL,12,Fstation in Norfolk.                    
OL,14,FWhen sentencing Goddard on Monday at   
OL,15,Fthe Old Bailey, Mrs Justice McGowan    
OL,16,Fsaid: "I find there is a continuing and
OL,17,Fserious risk."                         
